-- title:
--   Twisted weight is multiplicative on coprime pairs
-- statement:
--   For coprime nonzero natural numbers m and n, the twisted one-variable weight at the product m * n equals the product of the twisted weights at m and at n. The twisted weight is the product over prime divisors of the local good-choice count divided by Euler's totient, and both factors are multiplicative on coprime pairs. This is an unconditional, elementary multiplicativity statement; it claims no asymptotic main term. Formalization Note: the statement is written out in Mathlib terms, with no local definitions.
